                                 #|Profiler::now_us F0;i!Profiler; TFTFTFF
                                 #|Profiler::NowUs F0;i- TFFFFFF
                                 #|# Current bump-heap pointer (bytes) — the allocation analog of now_us,
                                 #|# for per-phase memory attribution in profiles/benches.
                                 #|Profiler::heap_bytes F0;i!Profiler; TFTFTFF
                                 #|Profiler::HeapBytes F0;i- TFFFFFF
                                 #|sleep F1;iu!Async; TFTTFFF
                                 #|# #1227: same host import as `sleep`, but row-free -- see
                                 #|# checker/builtin_sigs/builtins_system.vibe for why the row cannot be discharged.
                                 #|sleep_blocking F1;iu- TFTTFFF
                                 #|# ADR-0089 step 4 (#1218): raw halves of `host_future_get` (the checker
                                 #|# surface lives in checker/builtin_sigs/builtins_async.vibe; compile_call lowers it to
                                 #|# a [state=2, handle] future cell over vibe_hf_get_raw). Both are
                                 #|# codegen-internal (checker_visible=false): user source never spells
                                 #|# them, they appear only in injected AST (the entry boundary's
                                 #|# `__entry_settle`) and the compile_call lowering. They lower to the
                                 #|# `vibe.host_future_get` / `vibe.host_future_wait` host imports, which
                                 #|# only the component adapter module provides (spec §3.13/§3.14) -- a
                                 #|# plain-wasm host has no waitable machinery to implement them with.
                                 #|vibe_hf_get_raw F0;i- TFFTFFF
                                 #|vibe_hf_wait_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #1537: the group-wide half of the wait. `vibe_hf_arm_raw(h)` joins a
                                 #|# pending host future to the adapter's shared waitable set (1 = its value
                                 #|# already landed, 0 = armed); `vibe_hf_wait_any_raw()` blocks until one
                                 #|# armed future lands and returns its handle, whose value
                                 #|# `vibe_hf_wait_raw` then takes without blocking. Codegen-internal like the
                                 #|# pair above: they appear only as the bodies linked_compile gives
                                 #|# @vibe/concurrent's `__conc_host_*` hooks.
                                 #|vibe_hf_arm_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|vibe_hf_wait_any_raw F0;i- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #1537: the stream counterpart of vibe_hf_arm_raw -- start a one-byte read
                                 #|# of a host stream and join it to the shared set (1 = the next
                                 #|# vibe_hs_read_raw answers without blocking, 0 = armed).
                                 #|vibe_hs_arm_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #1537: start a timer of `ms` in the same shared set, so a group with
                                 #|# sleeping tasks and host waiters wakes at whichever comes first (its id,
                                 #|# a never-repeating n + 4096, when pending; 1 = already over). Its completion is
                                 #|# named by that id.
                                 #|vibe_hf_sleep_arm_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|vibe_hf_sleep_cancel_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #1537: nobody waits on this host future any more (its last waiting task
                                 #|# was cancelled): cancel its pending read and release the readable end.
                                 #|vibe_hf_cancel_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #1537: the only task that could read this host stream was cancelled:
                                 #|# cancel its armed read and release the readable end.
                                 #|vibe_hs_cancel_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #2066: append one byte to the component adapter's argument buffer, which
                                 #|# the next `wit_response_arg_get$` getter lowers as its string parameter.
                                 #|vibe_hf_arg_push_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|vibe_hs_claim_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# ADR-0089 Decision 3 (#1218): the shared READ half of the named host
                                 #|# streams (`host_stream_named` / `host_stream_next`, spec §3.18) -- one
                                 #|# byte per call, -1 at end of stream. Codegen-internal like the vibe_hf_*
                                 #|# pair above: appears only in the injected `__entry_settle` stream arm,
                                 #|# lowers to the `vibe.host_stream_read` host import that only the
                                 #|# component adapter provides. The per-name GET halves
                                 #|# (`vibe_hs_get_raw$<name>`) are program-minted and registered
                                 #|# dynamically in linked_compile, exactly like `vibe_hf_get_raw$<name>`.
                                 #|vibe_hs_read_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# ADR-0089 Decision 3 follow-up (#1218): the shared CLOSE half. Releases
                                 #|# the readable end of a host stream the guest stopped reading before end
                                 #|# of stream (`host_stream_close`, spec §3.18) -- the read half only drops
                                 #|# the end when it reaches EOS, so a partially consumed stream used to
                                 #|# hold its handle for the component instance's whole lifetime. Same
                                 #|# codegen-internal shape as the read half (injected `__hs_close` only),
                                 #|# and NOT async: dropping a readable end never blocks.
                                 #|vibe_hs_close_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# #1539 checker-hidden stdin provider core route. The component adapter
                                 #|# owns the canonical stream plus completion future behind an opaque ID.
                                 #|vibe_stdin_provider_acquire_raw F0;i- TFFTFFF
                                 #|vibe_stdin_provider_read_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|vibe_stdin_provider_close_raw F1;ii- TFFTFFF
                                 #|# Public source surface over that exact route. The unspellable CtStruct
                                 #|# identity prevents Int/HostStream/user types from forging a handle; the
